    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d502">

                <pb facs="0867" n="735" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg735"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860c.01/7–545: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 502<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-05T21:00:00+03:00">July 5, 1945—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2419. I delivered this evening to the Polish Amb
                    the texts of the President’s message to Osóbka-Morawski and of the public statement re the recognition
                    of the Polish Provisional Govt of National Unity (ReDeptel 1505, July 3, 4 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d502-f1"/>) the
                    Polish Amb expressed his appreciation for being
                    provided with these texts and stated that he would <pb facs="0868" n="736"
                        xml:id="pg736"/> transmit them to his govt immediately and that the
                    announcement of recognition would appear in tomorrow’s morning papers in
                    Poland.</p>
                <p>The Brit Amb is also sending a communication to
                    the Polish Amb this evening.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
